Feature: Update volume paths in pyspark_script.py using volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx

  The pyspark_script.py must be updated so that only the volume paths for biomarker_readings.csv, patient_demographics.csv, and site_details.csv are replaced with their corresponding new paths as specified in volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx. All other code, logic, and variable names must remain unchanged.

  Background:
    Given pyspark_script.py contains the following volume paths:
      | old_volume_path                                                                                   |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv               |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/patient_demographics.csv             |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/site_details.csv                     |
    And volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx contains the following mappings:
      | old_volume_path                                                                                   | new_volume_path                                                                                                 |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv               | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Biomarker.csv                  |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/patient_demographics.csv             | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Patient_Demographics.csv       |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/site_details.csv                     | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Site_Data.csv                  |

  Scenario: Happy path - All volume paths are replaced as per mapping sheet
    Given pyspark_script.py contains all three old volume paths
    When the script is updated using the mapping from volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx
    Then the following volume paths in pyspark_script.py must be replaced:
      | old_volume_path                                                                                   | new_volume_path                                                                                                 |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv               | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Biomarker.csv                  |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/patient_demographics.csv             | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Patient_Demographics.csv       |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/site_details.csv                     | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Site_Data.csv                  |
    And no other code, logic, or variable names are changed in pyspark_script.py

  Scenario Outline: Error scenario - Old volume path not found in mapping sheet
    Given pyspark_script.py contains the volume path "<old_volume_path>"
    And volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx does not contain a mapping for "<old_volume_path>"
    When the script is updated using the mapping sheet
    Then an error is raised with message "No mapping found for volume path: <old_volume_path>"

    Examples:
      | old_volume_path                                                                                   |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/unknown_file.csv                      |

  Scenario Outline: Error scenario - New volume path is empty in mapping sheet
    Given volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx contains a mapping for "<old_volume_path>" with an empty new_volume_path
    When the script is updated using the mapping sheet
    Then an error is raised with message "New volume path is empty for: <old_volume_path>"

    Examples:
      | old_volume_path                                                                                   |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv               |

  Scenario: Validation - Only volume paths are changed
    Given pyspark_script.py contains code logic, variable names, and three volume paths
    When the script is updated using the mapping sheet
    Then only the volume paths are changed as per mapping
    And all other code logic and variable names remain unchanged

  Scenario Outline: Data-driven test for volume path replacement
    Given pyspark_script.py contains the volume path "<old_volume_path>"
    When the script is updated using the mapping sheet
    Then the volume path "<old_volume_path>" is replaced with "<new_volume_path>"
    And the format of the new volume path is "/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/<file_name>"
    And no other changes are made to the script

    Examples:
      | old_volume_path                                                                                   | new_volume_path                                                                                                 | file_name                                 |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv               | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Biomarker.csv                  | 19_03_2025_Biomarker.csv                  |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/patient_demographics.csv             | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Patient_Demographics.csv       | 19_03_2025_Patient_Demographics.csv       |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/site_details.csv                     | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Site_Data.csv                  | 19_03_2025_Site_Data.csv                  |

  Scenario: Validation - New volume paths are accessible
    Given the new volume paths are updated in pyspark_script.py
    When the script is executed in the target environment
    Then the files at the new volume paths must be accessible and readable
    And no FileNotFoundError or access error is raised

  Scenario: Validation - Data processing logic remains unchanged
    Given the script logic for data cleaning, aggregation, and joining is present
    When the volume paths are updated as per mapping
    Then the data processing logic, including handling of Biomarker_A, Biomarker_B, Biomarker_C, Patient_ID, and joins, remains unchanged

  Scenario: Validation - Output data structure remains unchanged
    Given the final output dataframe structure in pyspark_script.py
    When the volume paths are updated
    Then the output dataframe columns and structure remain unchanged:
      | Patient_ID | Age | Gender | Weight (kg) | Location | Site_Type | Avg_Biomarker_A | Avg_Biomarker_B | Avg_Biomarker_C |

  Scenario: Validation - Volume path format
    Given the new volume paths in the mapping sheet
    When the script is updated
    Then each new volume path must match the format:
      | Format                                                                                           |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/<file_name>.csv              |
    And <file_name> must be one of:
      | 19_03_2025_Biomarker.csv                  |
      | 19_03_2025_Patient_Demographics.csv       |
      | 19_03_2025_Site_Data.csv                  |
